WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.020 --> 00:01.720
[Disclaimer: Characters, locations, and all depicted events are fictional

3
00:01.740 --> 00:03.470
and for entertainment purposes only; viewer discretion is advised]

4
00:12.180 --> 00:17.460
[Your Third Series]

5
00:17.790 --> 00:19.670
But this man loves you very much.

6
00:23.500 --> 00:24.620
I think

7
00:24.760 --> 00:26.280
you should just say yes.

8
00:26.710 --> 00:28.700
Thinking about it already gives me a headache.

9
00:29.710 --> 00:30.770
It was me

10
00:33.190 --> 00:35.200
who sent those men to get rid of Sarm

11
00:35.890 --> 00:36.400
Oh.

12
00:43.150 --> 00:44.170
What the fuck is this shit, huh?!

13
00:47.800 --> 00:48.430
Jam!

14
00:48.430 --> 00:48.820
Jam.

15
00:49.330 --> 00:50.190
That bastard did this to you?

16
01:00.600 --> 01:01.630
Stop it, Thee!

17
01:01.630 --> 01:03.720
If you hurt Mr. Sarm in any way,

18
01:03.740 --> 01:04.670
I will shoot!

19
01:37.910 --> 01:38.800
How are you?

20
01:39.890 --> 01:40.900
Are you hurt?

21
01:43.610 --> 01:46.009
Why should you care at all, Uncle?

22
01:48.430 --> 01:51.180
I was the one who sent the men to get rid of your son.

23
01:54.720 --> 01:56.280
Because I know that

24
01:58.400 --> 02:00.120
at your core...

25
02:00.900 --> 02:02.180
you're not a bad guy.

26
02:08.490 --> 02:09.259
I...

27
02:10.940 --> 02:12.200
I'm truly sorry.

28
02:17.230 --> 02:19.050
I want to own Adisuan Farm.

29
02:20.800 --> 02:22.450
I've been wanting to own it for years now.

30
02:24.240 --> 02:25.610
Half a year ago,

31
02:26.850 --> 02:28.350
Sarm disappeared.

32
02:29.770 --> 02:31.370
Everyone knew that he was heartbroken

33
02:31.370 --> 02:33.140
and wouldn't return soon.

34
02:33.520 --> 02:35.400
So I used that opportunity

35
02:38.800 --> 02:40.140
to send men to hunt him down

36
02:40.560 --> 02:42.860
so that he'd be gone for good.

37
02:43.100 --> 02:45.060
Then, people would assume that

38
02:46.410 --> 02:47.720
Sarm was so hurt

39
02:48.670 --> 02:50.260
that he wanted to live by the sea forever

40
02:52.600 --> 02:54.350
and had gone missing.

41
02:55.820 --> 02:57.200
Once the plan came to fruition,

42
02:57.840 --> 02:59.650
Adisuan Farm would probably belong to me.

43
02:59.980 --> 03:02.750
No one is better suited to run Adisuan Farm than me.

44
03:03.250 --> 03:04.630
You also knew that

45
03:06.160 --> 03:07.550
when Sarm was still away,

46
03:07.570 --> 03:08.900
I embezzled money,

47
03:09.320 --> 03:10.700
falsified accounting records,

48
03:11.730 --> 03:13.170
and forged documents.

49
03:14.300 --> 03:16.920
I was trying to take over Adisuan Farm bit by bit,

50
03:24.060 --> 03:25.550
then Sarm came back.

51
03:27.800 --> 03:29.390
And weren't you aware that

52
03:31.000 --> 03:32.140
Sarm also knew?

53
03:35.490 --> 03:36.910
I found it strange myself.

54
03:41.900 --> 03:44.200
Why did he choose to leave me be despite knowing everything?

55
03:47.400 --> 03:49.070
Because my son

56
03:50.500 --> 03:52.480
valued the bond you two shared.

57
03:54.590 --> 03:56.030
Do you despise me, Uncle?

58
04:08.980 --> 04:10.500
Do I?

59
04:16.529 --> 04:17.720
I don't, actually.

60
04:21.470 --> 04:22.900
Whether or not...

61
04:26.310 --> 04:27.740
I'd forgive you, though?

62
04:31.080 --> 04:32.100
It's still too soon.

63
04:37.430 --> 04:39.070
Do you know what the consequences

64
04:39.080 --> 04:40.420
of your action are?

65
04:45.080 --> 04:47.010
Let this

66
04:48.610 --> 04:49.770
be a lesson to you.

67
04:56.010 --> 04:57.440
Every day

68
04:59.070 --> 05:00.950
is a chance to start over.

69
05:25.310 --> 05:26.450
Rest well.

70
05:55.110 --> 06:00.390
[Your Third Series]

71
06:10.550 --> 06:14.480
♫Still feeling lonely? Well, you've got me,♫

72
06:14.520 --> 06:18.960
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

73
06:19.680 --> 06:23.620
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

74
06:23.680 --> 06:28.380
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

75
06:28.830 --> 06:33.360
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

76
06:33.380 --> 06:37.820
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

77
06:37.950 --> 06:42.210
♫But when they make you blue,♫

78
06:42.260 --> 06:45.970
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

79
06:46.940 --> 06:51.610
♫I'm here to love you as myself, not as a surrogate♫

80
06:51.650 --> 06:55.400
♫Let me be your safe space when you need a break♫

81
06:55.430 --> 07:00.420
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

82
07:00.500 --> 07:04.970
♫At least being your third still counts♫

83
07:05.370 --> 07:09.920
♫I'm here to love you, no matter who left you with heartache♫

84
07:09.970 --> 07:13.630
♫Just let me heal your heart, lending you my aid♫

85
07:13.660 --> 07:18.770
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

86
07:18.800 --> 07:20.780
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

87
07:20.810 --> 07:24.010
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

88
07:24.030 --> 07:26.980
[Your Third Series]

89
07:27.140 --> 07:27.750
Jam.

90
07:27.750 --> 07:28.430
Mr. Sarm?

91
07:32.670 --> 07:33.409
Little Jam...

92
07:33.890 --> 07:34.180
Little Jam!

93
07:34.180 --> 07:35.110
Sarm, Sarm.

94
07:35.110 --> 07:36.390
Calm down, calm down.

95
07:36.630 --> 07:37.110
Song,

96
07:37.340 --> 07:38.360
is Little Jam safe?

97
07:38.360 --> 07:39.770
He is safe

98
07:40.250 --> 07:41.659
and has been treated.

99
07:43.480 --> 07:44.650
Rest easy, okay?

100
07:54.300 --> 07:56.360
He's in the waiting room right now.

101
07:57.560 --> 07:59.020
PiMai is trying to make him feel better.

102
08:01.610 --> 08:02.900
What time is it?

103
08:03.390 --> 08:04.760
It's almost 5 A.M.

104
08:06.340 --> 08:07.850
Am I hurt that badly?

105
08:08.560 --> 08:10.270
Why am I hospitalized?

106
08:11.170 --> 08:12.600
You're having another brain scan.

107
08:12.750 --> 08:13.370
Huh?

108
08:14.050 --> 08:15.360
It's to see if anything's wrong.

109
08:16.370 --> 08:17.510
Do I even have that thing?

110
08:19.710 --> 08:20.610
Knock, knock.

111
08:20.930 --> 08:22.300
Seems like you don't.

112
08:22.650 --> 08:24.690
That's why you were being so reckless.

113
08:25.050 --> 08:26.830
You almost lost your head, alright?

114
08:26.830 --> 08:27.900
Being my twin brother,

115
08:27.900 --> 08:29.270
you always scold me or say nasty things to me.

116
08:29.270 --> 08:31.510
I'm a tiger with nine lives, alright?

117
08:31.670 --> 08:32.190
Right.

118
08:32.809 --> 08:34.090
I don't go down that easily.

119
08:34.090 --> 08:35.230
I hope that's true.

120
08:35.230 --> 08:36.659
Come on, you already know

121
08:36.659 --> 08:37.620
that I'm...

122
08:38.010 --> 08:39.150
tough.

123
08:41.960 --> 08:43.159
You people don't sleep or what?

124
08:43.480 --> 08:44.720
You already knew it, didn't you?

125
08:49.160 --> 08:50.020
I did.

126
08:55.160 --> 08:56.150
You mean I'm handsome, right?

127
08:56.150 --> 08:57.380
Not that, damn it!

128
08:59.010 --> 09:01.390
You knew that it was Thee who sent men to hunt you down, right?

129
09:05.300 --> 09:05.960
Of course...

130
09:17.170 --> 09:18.180
Fine!

131
09:22.050 --> 09:22.950
I'll say it.

132
09:24.810 --> 09:26.530
I found out when I got captured the second time.

133
09:26.860 --> 09:27.710
That night...

134
09:27.710 --> 09:29.330
I came back to my place with Little Jam after dinner,

135
09:30.900 --> 09:32.130
and they were already waiting for me.

136
09:32.780 --> 09:33.970
Then, I thought to myself,

137
09:33.970 --> 09:36.750
"How can I trace this back to the person behind it?"

138
09:37.310 --> 09:38.990
So I pretended to let them capture me.

139
09:39.150 --> 09:40.650
They tried taking me to a deserted island,

140
09:40.910 --> 09:41.830
but I didn't let them.

141
09:41.830 --> 09:43.020
I fought back.

142
09:43.160 --> 09:44.110
I beat them up!

143
09:44.360 --> 09:45.050
Punched!

144
09:45.230 --> 09:46.040
Slammed!

145
09:46.140 --> 09:47.030
Hit!

146
09:47.150 --> 09:47.700
And punched!

147
09:47.700 --> 09:48.210
Mm!

148
09:48.480 --> 09:49.840
Then, they folded.

149
09:50.590 --> 09:51.950
They spit it out, telling me that

150
09:51.970 --> 09:52.900
it was Thee...

151
09:52.910 --> 09:53.960
who gave them the order.

152
09:55.160 --> 09:56.660
Curse you, Thee...

153
09:57.150 --> 09:58.500
If I hadn't been worried about Little Jam,

154
09:58.500 --> 09:59.660
I would've punched,

155
09:59.660 --> 10:00.490
hit,

156
10:00.490 --> 10:01.350
slammed,

157
10:01.350 --> 10:02.380
and punched them more!

158
10:02.590 --> 10:04.170
So luck was on their side, huh?

159
10:04.170 --> 10:05.130
Mm...

160
10:05.730 --> 10:06.700
So I quickly backtracked

161
10:06.910 --> 10:07.930
and jumped into the water.

162
10:08.330 --> 10:10.730
I swam, swam, swam.

163
10:10.970 --> 10:12.180
"Little Jam!

164
10:12.180 --> 10:13.390
Where are you, Little Jam?!"

165
10:13.550 --> 10:15.010
And I found him floating in the middle of the sea.

166
10:15.010 --> 10:15.910
I asked myself...

167
10:15.910 --> 10:17.430
"Would he be okay?"

168
10:17.550 --> 10:19.160
So I swam him back to the shore.

169
10:19.160 --> 10:20.360
We ended up on Ko Samui.

170
10:21.390 --> 10:22.570
As for them,

171
10:22.920 --> 10:23.790
I pressured

172
10:24.260 --> 10:25.160
and squeezed them

173
10:25.310 --> 10:27.050
until they became key witnesses

174
10:27.050 --> 10:28.760
that would then seal Thee's fate.

175
10:29.140 --> 10:30.810
I simply have to call them,

176
10:31.770 --> 10:33.550
and they will make a grand reveal!

177
10:33.820 --> 10:34.730
It'll be glorious!

178
10:34.890 --> 10:35.960
And majestic!

179
10:36.620 --> 10:37.530
Oh...

180
10:37.530 --> 10:38.690
But it was too little, too late.

181
10:38.690 --> 10:39.560
Sheesh...

182
10:39.750 --> 10:41.300
I didn't get to be the star of the show.

183
10:41.850 --> 10:42.750
It's because of you, Sib.

184
10:42.750 --> 10:43.950
You sent Little Jam on a mission like that.

185
10:43.950 --> 10:44.730
And how did it go?

186
10:45.270 --> 10:46.190
Just look at this mess...

187
10:47.310 --> 10:49.160
I didn't know that you knew.

188
10:49.830 --> 10:51.560
That's why I sent Jam to look for evidence

189
10:52.090 --> 10:53.670
so that we can do it by the book.

190
10:56.360 --> 10:57.870
I didn't know that you knew.

191
10:59.850 --> 11:01.610
You should've told me what you were doing.

192
11:01.940 --> 11:02.750
What about Dad?

193
11:03.100 --> 11:04.290
Did he know anything?

194
11:05.060 --> 11:06.630
He told me that

195
11:06.630 --> 11:08.360
Uncle Mai was his friend

196
11:08.360 --> 11:10.180
back when they served in the army in the South.

197
11:10.540 --> 11:12.570
Ever since Uncle Mai found you at the beach,

198
11:12.710 --> 11:14.340
he has always been keeping Dad posted.

199
11:14.930 --> 11:16.130
Uncle Mai...

200
11:16.650 --> 11:18.450
The owner of the seafood restaurant?

201
11:19.620 --> 11:20.890
I never knew that.

202
11:20.890 --> 11:22.110
Oh, Uncle Mai.

203
11:22.540 --> 11:24.270
Whoa... You were pretty slick.

204
11:24.470 --> 11:26.730
And if I knew that Dad knew,

205
11:27.230 --> 11:27.830
I wouldn't have sent Jam

206
11:27.840 --> 11:29.390
to bring you back in the first place.

207
11:32.900 --> 11:35.230
None of us ever talk to one another, do we?

208
11:39.130 --> 11:40.050
And what about you?

209
11:40.050 --> 11:40.620
Hm?

210
11:40.620 --> 11:42.390
Did you know anything at all?

211
11:45.390 --> 11:46.550
I think I kind of did,

212
11:46.600 --> 11:47.680
but...

213
11:48.610 --> 11:49.860
I wasn't sure.

214
11:49.860 --> 11:51.130
Thought so.

215
11:51.950 --> 11:52.760
And...

216
11:53.070 --> 11:54.690
And what are we going to do about Thee?

217
11:58.720 --> 11:59.920
I'm taking this all the way.

218
12:00.390 --> 12:02.130
Bad guys don't get happy endings.

219
12:03.220 --> 12:04.570
The word "forgiveness"

220
12:05.060 --> 12:06.010
is not

221
12:06.030 --> 12:07.160
in my dictionary!

222
12:07.830 --> 12:08.930
Don't teach me what it means either.

223
12:09.560 --> 12:11.960
Thee, who I loved like a brother

224
12:12.480 --> 12:13.760
and trusted with everything,

225
12:14.020 --> 12:15.110
is now but a ghost!

226
12:19.010 --> 12:21.260
And I don't want to see his face at Adisuan Farm again.

227
12:24.290 --> 12:25.830
You, my brother...

228
12:26.220 --> 12:27.330
love someone deeply when you do

229
12:27.330 --> 12:28.760
and despise the person when you hate them.

230
12:29.220 --> 12:30.650
You've always been like this since you were a kid.

231
13:03.130 --> 13:04.190
Normally,

232
13:04.190 --> 13:06.490
I'd rush to my little boy.

233
13:06.490 --> 13:08.740
But this isn't normal.

234
13:10.250 --> 13:11.390
I'm still upset with him.

235
13:11.650 --> 13:12.830
I've asked him time and time again,

236
13:12.830 --> 13:14.590
yet he always hides the truth from me.

237
13:15.890 --> 13:17.550
I won't just be mad at him for a week,

238
13:17.940 --> 13:18.770
because this time...

239
13:18.780 --> 13:20.830
I'll be mad at him for months! Just you wait!

240
13:21.140 --> 13:22.380
Why didn't you listen?!

241
13:22.940 --> 13:23.960
You're so stubborn!

242
13:26.620 --> 13:27.060
Mr. Sarm...

243
13:27.060 --> 13:28.020
Hold it right there!

244
13:34.470 --> 13:35.690
Not now.

245
13:57.290 --> 13:58.830
Your mission has ended.

246
13:59.540 --> 14:00.750
This evening...

247
14:00.750 --> 14:02.370
It's time for you to return to Bangkok.

248
14:07.490 --> 14:08.360
Understood.

249
15:41.500 --> 15:42.700
I'm here to return your glasses.

250
15:46.050 --> 15:47.110
Thank you.

251
15:54.780 --> 15:56.890
Your phone and your car key...

252
16:06.580 --> 16:07.380
Right.

253
16:08.110 --> 16:09.860
Your car will be brought over tomorrow.

254
16:10.940 --> 16:12.250
No need to drive it yourself.

255
16:12.930 --> 16:13.950
I'll have someone drive it to you.

256
16:14.610 --> 16:15.190
But...

257
16:15.190 --> 16:16.140
No buts.

258
16:24.100 --> 16:24.900
Hello.

259
16:27.020 --> 16:28.610
Escort Mr. Jam to his place.

260
16:31.790 --> 16:33.260
Drive as smoothly as you can.

261
16:35.580 --> 16:37.340
Do not go over 80 km/h.

262
16:39.820 --> 16:41.960
Report back to me once you reach the destination.

263
16:45.060 --> 16:47.230
Do not forget to warn him to wear a seat belt

264
16:48.620 --> 16:49.830
because he's just that stubborn.

265
16:51.480 --> 16:52.390
He refuses to listen.

266
16:59.780 --> 17:00.870
And don't eat

267
17:02.230 --> 17:03.560
instant noodles too often.

268
17:05.069 --> 17:07.160
Eat some actual food.

269
17:10.140 --> 17:11.050
Mm.

270
17:12.490 --> 17:14.359
Don't overwork yourself.

271
17:15.690 --> 17:17.410
Can't keep working round the clock like this.

272
17:17.849 --> 17:18.690
Get some rest.

273
17:21.450 --> 17:22.569
Wherever you go,

274
17:22.569 --> 17:24.410
keep your eyes peeled.

275
17:26.869 --> 17:27.849
I know that you've got this,

276
17:29.590 --> 17:30.910
but nobody's there to take care of you

277
17:32.590 --> 17:33.910
when you're living there alone.

278
17:43.120 --> 17:44.510
As for boiled crabs...

279
17:45.560 --> 17:47.220
the ones from here are the best.

280
17:55.500 --> 17:57.370
Do not forget to take care of yourself, too.

281
18:22.910 --> 18:26.630
I should be happy because I'm done with Mr. Sarm.

282
18:28.110 --> 18:29.960
But why is it the opposite?

283
18:57.390 --> 18:59.250
I haven't gotten to ask him to be my boyfriend

284
18:59.250 --> 19:02.080
or wrap myself up as his present.

285
19:02.510 --> 19:03.390
Why?

286
19:03.560 --> 19:04.760
Just why?

287
19:22.230 --> 19:23.960
Look...

288
19:25.710 --> 19:27.940
This is Mr. Croc, my beloved crocodile plush.

289
19:32.030 --> 19:33.520
I love him so much.

290
19:33.540 --> 19:35.800
Can I bring Mr. Croc to Pak Chong with me?

291
19:43.630 --> 19:45.180
Why did your boss send you here?

292
19:47.470 --> 19:49.770
To learn the ins and outs of this farm.

293
19:51.730 --> 19:53.190
Are you sure?

294
19:55.010 --> 19:56.360
Don't hide anything from me.

295
20:02.770 --> 20:03.560
Mm.

296
20:05.750 --> 20:06.860
Okay.

297
20:06.860 --> 20:08.110
I believe you.

298
20:24.420 --> 20:26.360
Are you sure you actually lost?

299
20:30.850 --> 20:31.770
Mm.

300
20:33.690 --> 20:35.070
Are you certain

301
20:35.510 --> 20:37.160
that you're not plotting anything?

302
20:41.550 --> 20:43.410
I am doing nothing.

303
20:45.810 --> 20:47.390
I'll give you one more chance.

304
20:47.650 --> 20:48.830
Spit it out.

305
20:51.820 --> 20:53.660
I said I wasn't plotting anything.

306
20:56.980 --> 20:57.810
Okay.

307
20:57.950 --> 20:59.630
But if I catch you lying,

308
21:00.150 --> 21:01.410
even if it's you,

309
21:01.780 --> 21:03.560
I won't let it slide.

310
21:05.380 --> 21:06.590
Why?

311
21:09.210 --> 21:11.380
If I really am hiding something from you...

312
21:13.710 --> 21:15.020
That was just a hypothetical situation

313
21:15.690 --> 21:16.990
and nothing else.

314
21:17.820 --> 21:19.160
I'd be furious.

315
21:19.160 --> 21:20.650
I'd be mad at you for a whole week.

316
21:29.830 --> 21:33.150
You can be mad at me for a week if you want,

317
21:34.970 --> 21:37.660
but you have to forgive me after that, okay?

318
21:49.410 --> 21:50.390
Look at you...

319
21:52.900 --> 21:53.920
What a mess.

320
22:01.690 --> 22:03.210
This man...

321
22:03.900 --> 22:05.650
He's worn out...

322
22:10.540 --> 22:11.430
Not that big of a deal.

323
22:11.430 --> 22:12.410
Huh?

324
22:12.940 --> 22:14.360
"Not that big of a deal?"

325
22:14.660 --> 22:16.380
You did this to yourself, Sarm.

326
22:16.760 --> 22:17.700
I think

327
22:19.330 --> 22:21.300
"not that big of a deal is different for everyone."

328
22:21.890 --> 22:23.330
Someone I trusted...

329
22:23.330 --> 22:24.950
sent his men to get rid of me.

330
22:26.360 --> 22:27.560
Ow...

331
22:29.430 --> 22:31.430
I think I've developed

332
22:31.430 --> 22:32.740
trust issues.

333
22:36.730 --> 22:38.140
I can no longer trust anyone.

334
22:42.670 --> 22:43.660
Hey...

335
22:43.970 --> 22:45.190
I'm sorry.

336
22:45.190 --> 22:46.110
I...

337
22:47.850 --> 22:49.790
I forgot about that.

338
22:51.300 --> 22:52.380
Listen...

339
22:54.210 --> 22:55.850
And out of nowhere,

340
22:57.740 --> 22:58.760
Little Jam...

341
22:59.510 --> 23:00.850
was sent here.

342
23:03.180 --> 23:04.030
I always

343
23:04.490 --> 23:05.960
had my suspicions about him.

344
23:06.730 --> 23:07.780
I asked

345
23:07.780 --> 23:08.970
what his goal was,

346
23:09.210 --> 23:10.890
but I never got an answer!

347
23:10.890 --> 23:13.160
He just kept dodging my questions...

348
23:14.700 --> 23:16.420
I asked him so many times, too.

349
23:17.670 --> 23:19.890
He had no intention of hiding it from you, Sarm.

350
23:20.190 --> 23:20.990
It's Sib.

351
23:21.260 --> 23:23.370
He was following our big brother's order.

352
23:24.220 --> 23:24.820
Listen.

353
23:24.990 --> 23:25.850
I'm

354
23:26.550 --> 23:28.150
upset at both of them.

355
23:30.350 --> 23:32.070
But I'm mad at them for different reasons.

356
23:34.550 --> 23:35.750
Look at this plush.

357
23:36.810 --> 23:37.860
Just look at it.

358
23:39.940 --> 23:41.210
It's staring at me like this.

359
23:41.210 --> 23:42.190
I'm in this state,

360
23:42.190 --> 23:43.160
and yet you dare stare at me?

361
23:43.160 --> 23:45.010
You dare keep staring at me?

362
23:45.010 --> 23:45.940
What?!

363
23:45.940 --> 23:47.030
Got beef with me?!

364
23:47.330 --> 23:48.710
You're not going to feel sorry

365
23:48.710 --> 23:50.020
or show any remorse at all?

366
23:50.020 --> 23:51.150
What is it, huh?!

367
23:51.740 --> 23:52.680
How do you want to settle this?!

368
23:55.850 --> 23:56.610
What was that for?

369
23:58.510 --> 23:59.360
Go away.

370
24:00.570 --> 24:02.100
But with Little Jam, you see...

371
24:02.100 --> 24:02.360
Mm.

372
24:02.360 --> 24:03.560
I...

373
24:04.050 --> 24:05.680
I didn't quit trying.

374
24:07.200 --> 24:09.260
My feelings toward him haven't changed.

375
24:11.570 --> 24:12.890
I'm just confused.

376
24:18.570 --> 24:19.350
But...

377
24:20.160 --> 24:21.110
Why did he...

378
24:21.110 --> 24:23.060
He didn't even try to make it up to me?

379
24:26.220 --> 24:27.950
You want Jam to make it up to you?

380
24:30.700 --> 24:32.100
But you always looked...

381
24:32.100 --> 24:33.930
extremely unfriendly toward him.

382
24:34.610 --> 24:35.380
Gosh...

383
24:35.380 --> 24:36.870
Given the situation,

384
24:37.520 --> 24:39.080
how am I supposed to keep smiling?

385
24:39.410 --> 24:40.760
I can't.

386
24:46.760 --> 24:47.960
I simply can't.

387
24:48.780 --> 24:50.060
And what are you feeling exactly?

388
24:50.590 --> 24:51.380
Are you angry?

389
24:51.850 --> 24:52.760
Furious?

390
24:53.010 --> 24:53.960
Sad?

391
24:55.160 --> 24:56.670
Or upset?

392
25:07.140 --> 25:08.060
All of the above.

393
25:08.060 --> 25:08.710
Mm.

394
25:08.980 --> 25:09.560
I...

395
25:09.630 --> 25:10.630
I don't know.

396
25:10.940 --> 25:12.380
I'm feeling all of them at once.

397
25:12.770 --> 25:14.500
If I were a bowl of spicy salad,

398
25:14.500 --> 25:16.430
I'd be one with everything in it.

399
25:16.830 --> 25:18.370
Even if I got mad at him,

400
25:19.950 --> 25:21.350
he wouldn't make it up to me.

401
25:24.080 --> 25:25.160
I'm so upset...

402
25:35.170 --> 25:36.650
You love Jam, don't you?

403
25:36.980 --> 25:38.360
Of course, I do.

404
25:39.300 --> 25:40.490
I love Little Jam.

405
25:41.490 --> 25:42.970
I love him so much.

406
25:43.620 --> 25:45.150
I love him more than anyone.

407
25:46.890 --> 25:47.770
Hey.

408
25:47.770 --> 25:48.980
I, Traiphop,

409
25:49.390 --> 25:50.940
love Jiranat

410
25:52.460 --> 25:53.770
forever.

411
25:54.650 --> 25:55.900
If you love him,

412
25:56.830 --> 25:58.370
why did you let your emotions

413
25:58.900 --> 26:00.220
take over?

414
26:03.560 --> 26:04.760
What should I do, then?

415
26:05.730 --> 26:06.980
If I were you,

416
26:08.150 --> 26:10.410
I wouldn't wait around any longer.

417
26:11.130 --> 26:12.710
We're all grownups now.

418
26:13.430 --> 26:15.090
Don't complicate things.

419
26:16.390 --> 26:17.960
If you miss him,

420
26:18.380 --> 26:19.420
just say it.

421
26:19.980 --> 26:21.410
If you want to hear his voice,

422
26:22.630 --> 26:24.220
just call him.

423
26:25.770 --> 26:26.780
Or...

424
26:27.150 --> 26:28.550
If you want to see him,

425
26:29.270 --> 26:30.780
just go see him.

426
26:31.270 --> 26:32.540
It's as simple as that.

427
26:38.710 --> 26:39.560
Mm...

428
26:40.270 --> 26:41.380
Thank you very much, Song.

429
26:43.160 --> 26:44.750
It's like you've experienced it before.

430
26:46.410 --> 26:47.670
Who did that to you?

431
26:47.670 --> 26:48.540
It's okay.

432
26:48.540 --> 26:49.660
You've still got me.

433
26:49.660 --> 26:50.690
Listen, I'm right here.

434
26:50.690 --> 26:51.230
I'm here...

435
26:51.230 --> 26:51.970
- Let me kiss you. - It's okay...

436
26:51.970 --> 26:53.390
- I'm good... - Come here.

437
26:53.730 --> 26:54.220
Stupid Sarm.

438
26:54.220 --> 26:56.360
You should feel sorry about yourself first.

439
26:58.580 --> 26:59.960
Take a look at yourself.

440
27:02.480 --> 27:03.570
You're like a wet dog.

441
27:09.690 --> 27:11.750
Aunt Nim made you five-spice stew in a tiffin box.

442
27:11.750 --> 27:12.660
Don't forget to eat the stew.

443
27:12.660 --> 27:13.550
Right.

444
27:13.820 --> 27:14.360
You can go now.

445
27:14.360 --> 27:15.270
See you.

446
27:17.270 --> 27:18.420
What is it now?

447
27:20.310 --> 27:20.810
What's wrong?

448
27:20.810 --> 27:22.530
You didn't tell me sweet dreams.

449
27:22.630 --> 27:23.390
"Sweet dreams"?

450
27:23.620 --> 27:24.640
Am I Jam or what?

451
27:25.330 --> 27:26.360
Don't mention that name.

452
27:26.360 --> 27:28.300
There, there, there.

453
27:28.300 --> 27:29.250
It's okay. It's okay.

454
27:29.250 --> 27:29.960
Okay, well, then...

455
27:29.960 --> 27:31.160
Sweet dreams.

456
27:31.160 --> 27:32.360
Good night, good night.

457
27:32.360 --> 27:33.270
Okay...

458
27:33.270 --> 27:33.910
Good night.

459
27:34.530 --> 27:35.430
Bye-bye.

460
27:35.960 --> 27:37.050
I'm leaving now, okay?

461
27:39.410 --> 27:40.410
See you, alright?

462
27:44.360 --> 27:45.560
Again?

463
27:45.560 --> 27:47.030
You've stopped kissing me on the head.

464
27:47.030 --> 27:47.960
A kiss on my head! Come on!

465
27:47.960 --> 27:48.580
A kiss on your head?

466
27:49.900 --> 27:51.350
You used to do it every night.

467
27:51.350 --> 27:51.970
Fine, come here.

468
27:51.970 --> 27:52.760
Here comes a kiss on the head.

469
27:52.760 --> 27:55.760
Here comes your kiss on the head...

470
27:58.060 --> 27:58.760
Better now?

471
27:58.760 --> 28:00.130
Yes, you can leave now...

472
28:00.130 --> 28:01.160
- Better? - Mm.

473
28:03.220 --> 28:04.140
Bye-bye.

474
28:04.140 --> 28:06.510
You've been extremely weird since you were a kid.

475
28:06.660 --> 28:07.870
Don't forget that

476
28:07.870 --> 28:10.040
we're twins.

477
28:10.590 --> 28:11.470
If I'm weird,

478
28:11.470 --> 28:12.940
then so are you.

479
28:14.900 --> 28:15.890
Oh, you.

480
28:16.200 --> 28:17.440
You, of all people...

481
28:17.960 --> 28:18.960
are such a pain.

482
28:19.370 --> 28:20.230
Damn you, Sarm!

483
28:20.230 --> 28:20.650
Bye.

484
28:20.650 --> 28:21.330
I'm leaving for real now.

485
28:21.330 --> 28:22.290
Right.

486
28:27.430 --> 28:29.960
I miss you, Little Jam!

487
28:31.160 --> 28:32.140
Little Jam...

488
28:34.450 --> 28:35.980
I miss you...

489
28:36.420 --> 28:37.670
Little Jam.

490
28:38.150 --> 28:39.390
Oh, Little Jam...

491
28:39.670 --> 28:40.760
Little Jam...

492
28:41.070 --> 28:43.160
Little Jam, I miss you.

493
28:43.160 --> 28:44.480
Little Jam...

494
28:45.560 --> 28:46.760
Little Jam!

495
28:48.510 --> 28:49.160
Whoa.

496
29:03.310 --> 29:05.360
This house is full of scary animals.

497
29:16.900 --> 29:18.390
Little Jam!

498
29:47.680 --> 29:49.140
Your house is very lovely, you know?

499
29:51.380 --> 29:54.700
♫I came this far just to meet you♫

500
29:54.700 --> 30:01.510
♫There's so much you've been through♫

501
30:01.510 --> 30:04.900
♫But that doesn't matter♫

502
30:04.900 --> 30:08.210
♫Time stood still when I met you♫

503
30:08.210 --> 30:11.620
♫The way you gazed at me too♫

504
30:13.160 --> 30:14.590
Are you hitting on me?

505
30:14.790 --> 30:16.390
Yes, just now realizing that?

506
30:35.510 --> 30:38.780
♫I came this far just to meet you♫

507
30:38.780 --> 30:45.560
♫There's so much you've been through♫

508
30:45.560 --> 30:49.020
♫But that doesn't matter♫

509
30:49.020 --> 30:52.380
♫Mend your heart, make it better♫

510
30:52.380 --> 30:55.710
♫Whatever it is, you don't need to fear,♫

511
30:55.710 --> 31:02.500
♫For I'll be right here by your side like always♫

512
31:02.500 --> 31:08.770
♫It seems like something's moving♫

513
31:08.770 --> 31:15.330
♫What's in my heart isn't too much, but I only♫

514
31:16.210 --> 31:17.700
You silly...

515
31:18.390 --> 31:21.090
I already miss you just watching this.

516
31:21.700 --> 31:23.270
Everything looks perfectly normal.

517
31:29.400 --> 31:30.210
Little Jam!

518
31:30.230 --> 31:30.700
Whoa, Mr. Sarm?!

519
31:30.700 --> 31:31.850
- Little Jam! - How did you get here?

520
31:32.910 --> 31:33.390
Little Jam...

521
31:33.390 --> 31:34.760
Hey...

522
31:36.860 --> 31:38.900
No matter what I do,

523
31:40.020 --> 31:41.960
where I go,

524
31:42.160 --> 31:43.810
or where I look,

525
31:45.380 --> 31:47.750
I always see his face.

526
32:03.810 --> 32:05.410
Juju.

527
32:06.310 --> 32:08.130
What should I do?

528
32:10.760 --> 32:13.620
I cannot stop thinking about Mr. Sarm.

529
32:55.570 --> 32:57.130
How are you guys doing?

530
33:00.710 --> 33:01.960
Why did you ask that question?

531
33:02.590 --> 33:03.910
So what if I'm doing well?

532
33:04.090 --> 33:05.500
And what if I'm not?

533
33:05.830 --> 33:07.780
Are you going to cut my salary?

534
33:09.040 --> 33:10.480
I'd like to make it clear that

535
33:10.500 --> 33:12.720
I will not let you cut my salary.

536
33:13.780 --> 33:15.560
The only thing that can be cut

537
33:16.180 --> 33:18.330
is my love for you!

538
33:19.160 --> 33:20.990
You can't just be hangry and take it on me.

539
33:23.170 --> 33:23.890
Anything else you want?

540
33:23.910 --> 33:24.530
It's on me.

541
33:24.850 --> 33:26.150
No need to treat me to anything, Sarm.

542
33:26.810 --> 33:27.810
Why is that?

543
33:28.000 --> 33:29.720
It's because I can treat myself.

544
33:31.500 --> 33:32.870
Right...fantastic.

545
33:35.650 --> 33:37.160
Do you love Jam, Sarm?

546
33:39.560 --> 33:40.210
Yes,

547
33:40.740 --> 33:41.640
I love Jam.

548
33:46.340 --> 33:47.670
I knew it...

549
33:49.540 --> 33:51.110
The night at the New Year party,

550
33:51.730 --> 33:53.960
when you two kissed,

551
33:55.450 --> 33:57.410
I accidentally saw it.

552
34:00.950 --> 34:01.620
Mm...

553
34:01.950 --> 34:03.190
It has been clear since then.

554
34:04.070 --> 34:05.950
Tell Jam to shower you with love

555
34:07.530 --> 34:09.790
and love you as much as I've been hurt!

556
34:15.409 --> 34:16.500
Are you okay?

557
34:17.409 --> 34:18.370
It doesn't matter anymore.

558
34:18.980 --> 34:20.960
It's okay if our love got cut short.

559
34:20.980 --> 34:23.370
At least my priority was making good memories together,

560
34:23.570 --> 34:24.889
even if you didn't choose me.

561
34:26.620 --> 34:28.190
I'll have to take my leave now.

562
34:31.830 --> 34:33.560
Then I'll go with him.

563
34:33.699 --> 34:34.760
Wait, Mr. Wasin.

564
34:35.210 --> 34:36.760
You invited me here.

565
34:36.860 --> 34:37.790
And...

566
34:39.020 --> 34:41.110
Since when am I out of the loop?

567
34:42.090 --> 34:43.159
Uh...

568
34:43.159 --> 34:45.980
Back at the New Year party,

569
34:46.870 --> 34:48.560
Lantao dressed as a medium

570
34:48.650 --> 34:50.010
to exorcise ghosts.

571
34:50.550 --> 34:52.090
But he exorcised the wrong ghost.

572
34:52.550 --> 34:53.449
I'll be seeing you soon.

573
34:53.449 --> 34:54.260
Oh...

574
34:57.240 --> 34:58.360
This is just great.

575
34:59.500 --> 35:01.580
Lantao

576
35:02.110 --> 35:03.560
is about to make history.

577
35:08.100 --> 35:08.830
Oh?

578
35:10.070 --> 35:11.030
Oh, Ning-nong.

579
35:11.030 --> 35:12.730
I have something to tell you, Sarm.

580
35:13.020 --> 35:13.990
What is it?

581
35:14.670 --> 35:15.230
So...

582
35:15.240 --> 35:17.530
Someone's asking about buying the horse again.

583
35:18.370 --> 35:19.830
The horse's got serious charm,

584
35:19.830 --> 35:21.220
like the one who raised it.

585
35:22.860 --> 35:23.890
I'm not selling it.

586
35:52.150 --> 35:54.190
Would you like to have dinner now, Mr. Sarm?

587
35:57.110 --> 35:58.420
What's for dinner?

588
35:58.610 --> 35:59.740
There's rice porridge,

589
35:59.740 --> 36:01.370
stir-fried morning glory,

590
36:01.620 --> 36:03.150
salted squid heads,

591
36:03.420 --> 36:04.760
spicy salad with salted eggs,

592
36:05.170 --> 36:06.330
roasted prawns glazed with toddy palm sugar,

593
36:06.350 --> 36:08.360
and sweet fried dried fish.

594
36:12.930 --> 36:14.180
I'll have fried rice with crabs.

595
36:15.030 --> 36:15.940
Absolutely.

596
36:15.940 --> 36:17.180
I'll prepare it right away.

597
36:22.510 --> 36:23.880
We're all grownups now.

598
36:24.780 --> 36:26.740
Don't complicate things.

599
36:27.790 --> 36:30.270
If you miss him, just go see him.

600
36:30.270 --> 36:31.850
It's as simple as that.

601
36:37.160 --> 36:38.360
If I miss him...

602
36:38.830 --> 36:39.910
I should go see him?

603
36:41.710 --> 36:42.270
Aunt.

604
36:42.270 --> 36:42.890
Yes?

605
36:42.890 --> 36:44.140
I'll have dinner later.

606
36:44.850 --> 36:45.890
"If I miss him...

607
36:45.910 --> 36:46.760
I should go see him."

608
36:46.970 --> 36:48.590
"If I miss him... I should go see him."

609
36:48.590 --> 36:49.550
I miss him!

610
36:49.660 --> 36:50.660
I miss him!

611
36:50.940 --> 36:52.060
I miss him!!

612
37:23.230 --> 37:24.230
Juju!

613
37:24.470 --> 37:25.690
Is that you, Juju?

614
37:26.110 --> 37:27.230
Juju, it's your papa.

615
37:27.940 --> 37:28.970
I've come in peace.

616
37:29.190 --> 37:30.230
Juju!

617
37:31.890 --> 37:33.790
How was your time at the cat hotel, Juju?!

618
37:33.790 --> 37:35.480
Do you want to take a trip to Pak Chong?!

619
37:35.610 --> 37:36.860
We've got horses

620
37:36.860 --> 37:37.740
and goats.

621
37:38.130 --> 37:39.560
You'll get to go on a trip with us!

622
37:39.700 --> 37:40.760
Juju!

623
37:42.900 --> 37:43.420
Oh, Juju!

624
37:43.430 --> 37:44.540
Don't say no just yet!

625
37:44.540 --> 37:45.850
Turn around, please!

626
37:45.850 --> 37:47.170
Help me out, please!

627
37:49.270 --> 37:50.360
Juju...

628
37:51.680 --> 37:52.390
Jam.

629
37:57.560 --> 37:58.410
Jam...

630
37:58.760 --> 37:59.550
Little Jam!

631
37:59.670 --> 38:00.740
Little Jam!

632
38:03.870 --> 38:04.370
Ow...

633
38:04.500 --> 38:05.350
Little Jam,

634
38:05.960 --> 38:07.010
it's me, Sarm.

635
38:08.540 --> 38:09.390
Am I missing him so much

636
38:09.400 --> 38:10.940
that I'm imagining him here?

637
38:10.940 --> 38:11.960
Little Jam!

638
38:12.170 --> 38:13.050
Give me a break.

639
38:14.010 --> 38:14.850
Little Jam!

640
38:15.300 --> 38:16.030
Little Jam!

641
38:16.030 --> 38:16.760
Ow...

642
38:17.130 --> 38:18.390
Come on, Juju.

643
38:18.710 --> 38:20.040
Shall we go to bed together?

644
38:20.360 --> 38:21.380
Little Jam!

645
38:22.870 --> 38:23.960
Little Jam!

646
38:24.670 --> 38:25.730
Little Jam!

647
38:26.100 --> 38:26.860
This is Sarm...

648
38:26.970 --> 38:28.100
It's me.

649
38:30.230 --> 38:31.550
- Mr. Sarm?! - Damn right!

650
38:31.930 --> 38:32.360
I mean, yes.

651
38:32.360 --> 38:33.560
It's me.

652
38:33.560 --> 38:34.940
- Wait, wait, wait. - Yes?

653
38:34.940 --> 38:35.960
What are you doing?!

654
38:36.530 --> 38:37.160
I'm...

655
38:37.370 --> 38:38.360
I'm here to see you, Little Jam.

656
38:38.360 --> 38:39.560
Gosh...

657
38:39.900 --> 38:40.760
Get off the gate...

658
38:40.760 --> 38:41.960
There's so little time left.

659
38:42.110 --> 38:42.950
I've got something to tell you.

660
38:42.950 --> 38:44.070
I

661
38:44.070 --> 38:44.980
miss

662
38:44.980 --> 38:45.990
you,

663
38:45.990 --> 38:47.030
Jam!

664
38:47.170 --> 38:48.170
Mr. Sarm!

665
38:48.170 --> 38:48.650
Little Jam...

666
38:48.670 --> 38:49.640
Get down from there right now.

667
38:49.860 --> 38:50.630
No...

668
38:50.630 --> 38:52.260
I can't wait any longer,

669
38:53.070 --> 38:54.530
not even another second.

670
38:54.530 --> 38:55.770
It feels heavy,

671
38:55.770 --> 38:56.850
